    "created_at": "2016-05-31T05:56:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T20:14:40Z",
    "body": "So, I was about to re-review this, but then I realized that we have https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/136 which seems similar (for canvas, not ImageBitmap) and there we called it \"imageSmoothingQuality\" and went with the values \"low\", \"medium\", and \"high\".\n\nAlthough maybe we should have caught that at the time and advised aligning with CSS's names of \"imageRendering\" and \"auto\", \"high-quality\", \"crisp-edges\", and \"pixelated\", we didn't. Maaaybe we could go back and change it, but I'd feel pretty bad, given that WebKit contributed the patch and [implemented already](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=149541).\n\nCan the domain experts weigh in with their thoughts? @tabatkins @fantasai as authors of https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-3/#the-image-rendering; @hober as the author of https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/136 and @grorg as he contributed to the discussion in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/98. And of course @junov and @xidachen.\n\nHere are my questions:\n- How do people feel about the CSS image-rendering values? I imagine they've been under a lot of discussion in the CSSWG, but are they final or shipping anywhere? Do the canvas people feel comfortable with them?\n- Is it important or desirable to unify between [CSS image-rendering](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-3/#the-image-rendering), Canvas [ImageSmoothingQuality](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#2dcontext:imagesmoothingquality-2), and the proposed-in-this-PR ImageBitmap resize filter?\n- If we want _do_ want to align all three, is WebKit willing to change ImageSmoothingQuality, despite having already implemented the existing values? (Our bad as spec editors for not bringing this up at the time...)\n- If we decide that ImageSmoothingQuality and CSS image-rendering are actually supposed to be different (as they are currently), what about ImageBitmap resize filter? Is it similar to CSS image-rendering, or to ImageSmoothingQuality, or is it a third thing?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
