    "created_at": "2016-06-09T20:07:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T20:07:57Z",
    "body": "I don't think it's very important to hew closely to the CSS naming here.  The CSS side is going more for a combination of value and intent semantic; this API is more directly \"how much effort do you want to spend smoothing this resize\".  At _most_, leaning on \"pixelated\" as the low-level value might be appropriate, but it's fine to just have that the default when smoothing isn't turned on.\n\n>  The \"auto\" vs. \"high-quality\" distinction is quite subtle and I'm unclear whether UAs actually plan to dynamically change the meaning of the keywords based on available system resources.\n\n`high-quality` was added at the request of the Apple people, who apparently _do_ have this semantic internally and wanted to expose it, so you could prioritize some images on the page as needing to be higher-quality than others and to degrade last when resources were constrained.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/225010955/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
