    "created_at": "2016-06-09T20:15:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T20:15:04Z",
    "body": "OK. In that case it might be best to go back to @xidachen's original proposal of  \"pixelated\", \"low\", \"medium\", and \"high\".\n\nShould we consider using the name imageSmoothingQuality, like canvas does? Or would that be too confusing because on canvas we use imageSmoothingEnabled = false, whereas on ImageBitmap we use imageSmoothingQuality = \"pixelated\"?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
