    "created_at": "2016-06-09T20:21:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T20:21:01Z",
    "body": "Yep, I agree. The bool is a worse API, and the only reason we have it for canvas is because the bool came first and then we added the enum later.\n\nThe question is, when creating this new API, which is isomorphic-to-but-different-from the canvas API, how do we reconcile the differences? It sounds like you are advocating for there being two separate concepts:\n- resizeQuality = { \"pixelated\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\" }\n- imageSmoothingQuality = { \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\" } with \"pixelated\" being controlled by an extra boolean\n\nThis might be the best solution. At least, I don't see any great solutions, so maybe this is the least-worst one.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
